---
import FlowShot from '../FlowShot.astro';
import FlowDetail from '../FlowDetail.astro';
import shotSmartRouting from '../../../assets/flow/shots/settings-smart-routing.webp';
import detailRoutingDecided from '../../../assets/flow/details/detail-routing-decided.webp';
import detailRoutingRules from '../../../assets/flow/details/detail-routing-rules.webp';
---
<section class="border-t border-border/60 px-6 py-14 sm:py-20" aria-labelledby="tour-routing">
  <div>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <p class="of-eyebrow" data-animate="rise">Smart Routing</p>
      <h3 id="tour-routing" class="of-display scroll-mt-28 mt-4 text-[clamp(1.85rem,3.4vw,2.75rem)]" data-animate="lead">Your rules choose. Flow shows why.</h3>
      <p class="of-lede mt-5" data-animate="rise">Rules decide in order; the first one that matches applies. Five built-in rules cover locality, document fit, price, and speed measured on this Mac. Duplicate one to make your own. The order stays fixed until you edit it.</p>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-text-muted">A rule with no qualifying model says so. Unmeasured models are not speed-ranked, missing prices are never guessed, and rules never judge answer quality.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="of-stage of-stage--pad-bottom mt-12" data-animate="plate">
      <FlowShot src={shotSmartRouting} alt="Flow's Smart Routing settings with ordered rules, live qualifying-model counts, and the rule-template menu open, beside a market landscape document." crop sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 78rem, (min-width: 1024px) 64rem, 100vw" />
      <FlowDetail class="of-stage__detail of-stage__detail--br" src={detailRoutingRules} alt="Flow's ordered Smart Routing rules with live counts, the Deciding badge on the first rule that matches, and Add Rule." caption="Rules decide in order · The first match applies" sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 30rem, (min-width: 1024px) 27rem, calc(100vw - 3rem)" animate />
    </div>
    <div class="mx-auto mt-12 grid max-w-5xl items-center gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[0.9fr_1.1fr]">
      <div>
        <p class="flow-path__num">Signed route</p>
        <h4 class="mt-2 text-xl font-bold">The model and the deciding rule stay together.</h4>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-muted">The same sentence appears wherever Flow previews a route: the model it would use, followed by “Decided by the rule.” Pin a model yourself and no rule takes credit.</p>
      </div>
      <FlowDetail src={detailRoutingDecided} alt="Flow naming the model Smart Routing would use and the rule that decided it." caption="Model named · Deciding rule named" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 36rem, calc(100vw - 3rem)" />
    </div>
    <p class="of-spec-fine mx-auto mt-8 max-w-3xl text-center uppercase tracking-[0.14em]">Captured 2026-08-26 on the installed release build 1255 (v1.5). The screen carries the route and its reason together.</p>
  </div>
</section>
